  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="150e11bb-e0a2-58bf-a112-6e7da1271329" activityNameId="04915e53-c34c-52d6-bc9f-ac8121c7bdac" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Discharge, produced water, offshore</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Discharge, produced water, offshore
Emissions related to discharge of produced water;
646fba6c-683b-303f-91d5-d0709295b79b
Emissions of water pollutants without water content discharged to rivers after treatment. Oil emissions are not included and are considered separately. Water in- and output have to be considered separately.
Location:  Data from literature for offshore production in the North Sea, Indonesia, Mexico , USA and Canada
Technology: Discharge after pre-treatment.
Time period: Time of publications. Most figures could be verified for 2011.
Production volume: About 1m3 of water is discharged per tonne of crude oil produced.
Sampling: Publication in environmental reports and other literature.
Extrapolations: Several measurements from platforms in different countries available. Applied on all offshore operations.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_646fba6c-683b-303f-91d5-d0709295b79b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="3320dcee-ac7b-51fa-8397-bc03eb397f03" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
